{"judgments": [
{"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
  {"issue": "Four separate lessors are each recited as \"acting in his/her sole and separate interest,\" which does not say whether each leases only an undivided share or whether they jointly lease the whole tract. Read with Paragraph 9's lesser-interest clause, the extent of what each Chambers lessor conveyed is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
]},
{"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The grant of the right to \"transport by pipelines or otherwise across and through said lands oil, gas and their constituents from the subject and other lands,\" surviving the lease term, cannot be squared with Paragraph 25 and Addendum ¶20, which deny Lessee any right to move gas from other lands across the premises. Which controls is sharpened by the Addendum priority clause.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.55},
  {"issue": "The premises are described both by enumerated tax parcels with stated acreages and by a catch-all covering \"all the property owned by Lessor or to which the Lessor may have any rights,\" \"containing 904.10 acres, more or less,\" a figure the listed parcels do not add up to. Whether the specific parcels or the general Mother Hubbard words bound the leasehold is a general-versus-specific question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
]},
{"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The habendum extends the term so long as gas is \"produced or are capable of being produced on the premises in paying quantities, in the judgment of the Lessee\"; \"capable of being produced\" and \"paying quantities\" are undefined and the measure is committed to Lessee's own judgment. Whether the lease survives without actual marketed production turns on that phrase.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32},
  {"issue": "The term is extended \"as provided in Paragraph 7 following,\" but Paragraph 7 addresses only the adequacy of consideration and Lessee's right to drill or not drill and says nothing about maintaining the term; the shut-in mechanism is in Paragraph 6. The cross-reference cannot be given effect as written.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
]},
